WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:12.525
It was a cloudy day.

2
00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:16.727
The kids looked out the window as they put on their aprons.

3
00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:20.968
"A storm is coming," Jason said.

4
00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:23.730
"Oh no!"

5
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:24.990
Izzie thought.

6
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.032
"Everyone, pay attention," Chef said.

7
00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:32.025
"We're making beef chili today."

8
00:00:33.726 --> 00:00:37.447
Outside, lightning flashed, followed by a rumble of thunder.

9
00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:40.649
Izzie clenched her teeth.

10
00:00:40.669 --> 00:00:44.430
"Yay! It's starting to rain!"

11
00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.591
Nina said.

12
00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:48.672
"The garden is getting watered!"

13
00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:51.473
Chef nodded.

14
00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.235
"Jason, please chop the onion.

15
00:00:55.335 --> 00:00:57.156
Izzie, you can chop the bell pepper.

16
00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:00.630
Bobby and Nina, you can chop the garlic."

17
00:01:03.552 --> 00:01:06.174
Izzie tried not to look out the window as she worked.

18
00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:10.497
When she was finished, she checked the recipe again.

19
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:14.720
"Next we cook the pepper and onion."

20
00:01:16.941 --> 00:01:20.144
Nina poured oil into a pot and added the pepper and onion.

21
00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:23.406
Bobby added the garlic.

22
00:01:24.727 --> 00:01:25.848
Lightning flashed again.

23
00:01:26.996 --> 00:01:30.078
Boom! This time the thunder was even louder.

24
00:01:30.098 --> 00:01:34.081
"Whoa!" Bobby said.

25
00:01:34.101 --> 00:01:38.444
"It's pouring now," Jason said.

26
00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.506
"What a cool storm!"

27
00:01:40.526 --> 00:01:44.548
"Stop talking about the thunderstorm!"

28
00:01:44.949 --> 00:01:45.769
Izzie snapped.

29
00:01:47.691 --> 00:01:49.072
Her friends looked surprised.

30
00:01:49.092 --> 00:01:54.936
"I mean, er we should be busy cooking!"

31
00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.557
Chef nodded.

32
00:01:57.577 --> 00:01:59.598
"Let's keep working.

33
00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:01.780
We have to brown the beef now."

34
00:02:04.762 --> 00:02:07.184
He used a spoon to break up the beef in the pot.

35
00:02:08.685 --> 00:02:11.447
While it cooked, Izzie opened the can of beans.

36
00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:16.190
Nina held a strainer, and Izzie poured the beans into it.

37
00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.813
"We drained the liquid," Izzie said.

38
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.856
"Next we rinse the beans and add them to the pot."

39
00:02:25.676 --> 00:02:28.657
"I'll add the can of tomatoes," Bobby said.

40
00:02:30.477 --> 00:02:31.558
Izzie looked at Chef.

41
00:02:31.578 --> 00:02:34.138
"Can we mix all the spices now?"

42
00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:37.839
"Sure. You're working fast today, Izzie."

43
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.080
Chef pointed to the spices on the counter.

44
00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.561
Izzie quickly measured the chili powder.

45
00:02:45.401 --> 00:02:47.062
She poured it into a small bowl.

46
00:02:48.782 --> 00:02:51.683
Nina and Jason added cumin and oregano.

47
00:02:53.103 --> 00:02:54.724
Bobby put in the paprika.

48
00:02:56.636 --> 00:02:59.178
"Now we add the salt and pepper," Izzie said.

49
00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.142
Nina mixed all the spices together.

50
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.646
Then Chef added the mix to the chili and stirred.

51
00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:12.550
"The chili simmers on low heat for twenty minutes," Jason said.

52
00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:15.853
"Right," Chef said.

53
00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:19.136
"The spices will add flavor as it simmers."

54
00:03:28.448 --> 00:03:29.429
Bobby smiled.

55
00:03:29.449 --> 00:03:33.031
"Let's tell ghost stories while we wait!"

56
00:03:34.612 --> 00:03:36.293
"No!" Izzie said.

57
00:03:36.313 --> 00:03:38.834
"We have to clean up first."

58
00:03:38.854 --> 00:03:45.057
"Yep." Jason started washing dishes.

59
00:03:45.078 --> 00:03:49.700
"I'll help you, Jason," Izzie said.

60
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.003
"We can all help with the chores," Chef said.

61
00:03:55.143 --> 00:03:56.304
He put on some music.

62
00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.841
Soon everyone was busy, cleaning up the kitchen.

63
00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.582
A few minutes later, a flash of lightning lit up the windows.

64
00:04:07.143 --> 00:04:09.263
A huge crack of thunder split the air.

65
00:04:10.704 --> 00:04:11.604
Jason jumped.

66
00:04:12.804 --> 00:04:14.365
"Yikes! That was loud!"

67
00:04:14.385 --> 00:04:19.686
"What?" Izzie looked up from the dish she was drying.

68
00:04:19.706 --> 00:04:22.747
"I didn't even hear it this time!"

69
00:04:24.508 --> 00:04:26.292
Chef grinned.

70
00:04:26.312 --> 00:04:27.973
"Sometimes it's good to stay busy."

71
00:04:29.555 --> 00:04:30.275
Izzie nodded.

72
00:04:30.295 --> 00:04:34.598
"Maybe I'll try it during the next thunderstorm," she thought.

73
00:04:36.159 --> 00:04:37.600
At last the timer went off.

74
00:04:39.242 --> 00:04:41.683
Chef filled five bowls with steaming chili.

75
00:04:43.184 --> 00:04:44.405
Nina looked out the window.

76
00:04:44.425 --> 00:04:47.007
"The storm is over!"

77
00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.709
Izzie sighed with relief.

78
00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.332
Then she blew on her chili to cool it off.

79
00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.163
"It's delicious!"

80
00:04:56.644 --> 00:04:58.006
she said, tasting it.

81
00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.834
A ray of sunshine shone through the window.

82
00:05:01.854 --> 00:05:03.778
"And look!

83
00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:05.081
There's a rainbow!"

84
00:05:05.502 --> 00:05:06.123
Izzie said.
